  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Health Systems - Health Workforce Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  USAID/Nigeria&apos;s buy-in to USAID&apos;s Integrated Health Systems (IHS) mechanism supports the establishment of a cost-effective, well-trained and motivated health workforce that will contribute to improved management of reproductive health, family planning, maternal, child and newborn health conditions and increased responsiveness to community health needs. .The activity offers a state-of-the-art approach for advancing Nigeria&apos;s health workforce agenda through tailored, state-level technical assistance. Interventions will target the focus states of Bauchi, Sokoto, Kebbi, Ebonyi, and the Federal Capital Territory ensuring that technical assistance meets context-specific priorities for local human resources and health systems. Interventions will focus on support to state governments to improve the quality of training for the health workforce, strengthen the health workforce information system, improve health workforce governance and management, and strengthen local capacity for learning, documentation, and research. With FY 2021 funds, the activity will support the establishment and strengthening of key human resources for health governance platforms,, strengthen continuing education systems and human resource information systems, provide technical assistance to develop and implement action plans, policies, and strategic plans to improve these training institutions and system platforms, and support initiatives to improve the availability of health workforce for primary health care service delivery. ...</narrative>
  </description>
